cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this hardware or its design files, please cite the HardwareX article."
title: "CPS-Sort: a low-cost, open-source cyber-physical sorting cell for real-time visual quality inspection on commodity hardware"
abstract: >-
  A conveyor-paced visual quality inspection cell that segments each component
  with YOLOv8s-seg on a passively cooled laptop CPU and deflects it into one of
  four bins with servo-driven arms, built for approximately US$1,548 from
  commodity components. This deposit holds the mechanical design files, the
  ESP32 firmware, the host application, the operator dashboard and the training
  script.
